hrough R15 to GND. This is reversed relative to every other LED in the FCC group, e.g. LED4 has its anode on LED_B_FCC and its cathode through R16 to GND.\", \"expected\": \"The anode should be on the MCU drive net and the cathode should return to GND through the 330 ohm resistor, as for LED4 and LED5.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"51\\\") (name \\\"LED_A_FCC\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"35\\\") (pinfunction \\\"PB1\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) (node (ref \\\"LED3\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"K\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"53\\\") (name \\\"LED_B_FCC\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"36\\\") (pinfunction \\\"PB2\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) (node (ref \\\"LED4\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")))\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"DLED3 LED_A_FCC Net-_LED3-A_ LED_D_R\"}], \"impact\": \"With its anode tied to GND through R15, LED3 cannot conduct for any drive level on PB1, so the status indicator is dead.\", \"confidence\": 0.45}], \"summary\": \"The NAVC1 MCU's VSS pins are isolated from GND and its VDD pins are unconnected, and LED3 is installed with reversed polarity compared with its neighbours. The NAVC power/ground fault is the most serious issue, though the design may have quirks I cannot verify from the netlist alone.\"}",
